WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:07.040
The best way to understand permutations and combinations

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.500
is by solving as many examples as possible.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.300
In this example,

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.880
we have been asked to arrange the letters of the word rock.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.900
In how many different ways,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.080
can the letters of the word rock be arranged?

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.540
We have one word,

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.240
and we need to rearrange the letters to form different arrangements.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.940
As rock has four letters, let's make four slots.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.380
What exactly are we asked for?

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.720
In how many ways can the letters be arranged?

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.680
We can form arrangements like 'ORKC',

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.480
or 'CROK' or 'KORC' and so on.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.740
How many such arrangements can we form?

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.280
If you have gone through our previous sessions,

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.640
you would Immediately realize that this problem is no different.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:58.840
It's like we have been given four different digits,

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.860
and asked for the number of four digit numbers that can be formed.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.600
Do we have any condition here? Nope!

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.840
We have simply been asked for the number of possible ways,

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.820
in which these letters can be rearranged.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.100
So we can start from anywhere.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.420
Say we start with the first slot.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.680
In how many ways can the first slot be occupied?

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:22.460
The word 'rock' has four letters.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:26.240
So the first slot can be filled with any of these four letters.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.720
Four ways.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.640
Now having filled the first slot,

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.880
in how many ways can the second slot be filled?

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.860
One of the letters has been used in the first slot.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.140
Three remain.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:40.180
The second slot can be filled in three ways.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.300
If we have used an 'O' in the first slot,

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:48.060
then we can use any one from R, C and K for the second slot.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.720
If we use a 'C' in the first slot,

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.180
then anyone from R, O and K can be used in a second.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.400
Now having filled the first and the second slot with one letter each,

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.580
in how many ways can the third slot be filled?

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.980
Two ways as just two letters would remain.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:08.800
And the fourth slot can be filled with just one way

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:12.140
as three letters have already been used up.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.160
Four ways in which we can fill the first slot.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.300
Three ways in which the second slot can be filled,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.440
two ways in which the third slot can be filled

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.700
and after having filled these three,

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.000
only one way in which the last slot can be filled.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.320
As we are filling the first and the second and the third and the fourth slot,

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.860
we multiply these four numbers to get the answer.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.620
24 different ways,

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.300
in which the letters of the word 'rock' can be arranged.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.080
And this is also four factorial.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.600
You could have written this answer directly

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:49.840
provided you understood how we arrived at it.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.500
The number of arrangements

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:55.980
or permutations of 'N' distinct objects is 'N' factorial.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:57.540
Indirectly,

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:01.780
this question asked us for the number of anagrams of the word 'rock'.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.120
And this includes all the meaningless ones as well!

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:09.420
Like 'OKRC', 'KROC' and so on.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.120
So this was easy!

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.000
Now let me ask you a similar question.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.380
How many different anagrams of 'mooc' can be formed?

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:22.820
'Mooc' stands for 'massive open online courses'.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.780
How many anagrams like

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:29.700
'MOCO', 'COOM' can be formed using the letters of 'mooc'?

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:35.020
Try it out and we will see the solution in the next session.

